=== Text #1 ===
> Level 2[ NV]Q Diploma in Wood Occupations (Timber Frame Erection) - Q2W Ltd.
The Level 2[ NV]Q Diploma in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection is designed to assess occupational competence in the workplace[.] Learners[ are] required to demonstrate their skills, knowledge and[ experience] in the construction of timber frame buildings[.] This qualification is suitable for practicing timber frame carpenters.
This[ NV]Q provides formal recognition of practicing as timber frame carpenter[.]
There are no formal entry requirements for this[ NV]Q qualification,[ however] the potential learner must be able to demonstrate that they can meet the skills, knowledge and experience requirements of the[ NV]Q in timber frame carpentry before[ enrol]ment.
The Level 2[ NV]Q Diploma in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection qualifies the holder to apply for the Construction Skills Certification[ Scheme] ([C]SC[S]) blue skill card (https[://]www.[csc]s.uk.com/card-type/manager/[).]

